# Example operator env for multi-hop *prep* (copy values out-of-band; do not commit secrets).
# Residual catalog peers (product monopin):
#   IS Iceland  82.221.101.241:44044
#   RO Romania  185.146.232.107:44044
#   DE Germany  167.233.224.5:44044
#
# Exit hop (second FlokiNET country — fill when VPS is ready):
# Romania exit hop (FlokiNET) — live when ready:
RPT_EXIT_HOST=185.146.232.107
RPT_EXIT_PORT=44044
# Germany residual peer (Hetzner FSN):
# RPT_DE_HOST=167.233.224.5
# RPT_DE_PORT=44044
# RPT_ENTRY_COUNTRY=DE
# RPT_EXIT_COUNTRY=Romania
# RPT_EXIT_ELGAMAL=new  # policy A — new exit-only keypair
# Entry remains 82.221.101.241:44044 (Iceland)
# RPT_EXIT_HOST=
# RPT_EXIT_PORT=44044
#
# Enable hop-list *config* only (not residual multi-hop routing):
# RPT_MULTIHOP_ENABLED=1
# RPT_MULTIHOP_HOPS=82.221.101.241:44044,185.146.232.107:44044
# RPT_SSH_HOST=185.146.232.107
# RPT_SSH_ROLE=exit_hop
#
# Deploy exit node over SSH:
# RPT_SSH_HOST=<EXIT_HOST>
# RPT_SSH_USER=raskul
# RPT_SSH_SUDO=1
# RPT_SSH_KEY=$HOME/.ssh/id_ed25519_restore_privacy_hop
# RPT_SSH_PASSWORD=   # one-time bootstrap only; prefer key auth
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private residual capacity probes (near-capacity client migration)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared secret for token-gated GET /api/private/capacity on residual nodes.
# Same value on **every residual node** (systemd) and on **operator clients**
# that should probe before residual dial. Do **not** commit real tokens.
# Missing token → probes off (empty map; no capacity migration from probes).
# Public /api/status stays title-only — never a live client counter.
#
# RPT_CAPACITY_TOKEN=replace-with-long-random-secret
# Optional soft max for utilization = live_sessions / max (node):
# RPT_NODE_MAX_SESSIONS=256
# Optional per-node bandwidth allowance (bits/s) — product budget, not NIC auto-detect:
# RPT_NODE_BANDWIDTH_CAP_BPS=100000000   # IS/RO 100 Mbps
# RPT_NODE_BANDWIDTH_CAP_BPS=200000000   # DE 200 Mbps
# Status host admin fleet panel: same token + cap map (host or country code → bps):
# RPT_BANDWIDTH_CAP_BPS_MAP={"82.221.101.241":100000000,"185.146.232.107":100000000,"167.233.224.5":200000000,"IS":100000000,"RO":100000000,"DE":200000000}
# Optional client probe URL map (JSON host → private capacity URL):
# RPT_CAPACITY_PROBE_URLS={"82.221.101.241":"http://82.221.101.241:8080/api/private/capacity","185.146.232.107":"http://185.146.232.107:8080/api/private/capacity","167.233.224.5":"http://167.233.224.5:8080/api/private/capacity"}
# Optional probe timeout seconds (default ~1.5):
# RPT_CAPACITY_PROBE_TIMEOUT=1.5
#
# Node install (root on residual VPS):
#   bash scripts/install_capacity_token_env.sh
#   # or with allowance:
#   # RPT_CAPACITY_TOKEN='…' RPT_NODE_BANDWIDTH_CAP_BPS=100000000 bash scripts/install_capacity_token_env.sh
# Client / status host (operator — same secret as nodes; never commit):
#   export RPT_CAPACITY_TOKEN='(same secret as nodes)'
# Docs: docs/CAPACITY_PROBES.md
